%I A399850 #4 Sep 17 2026 00:25:11
%S A399850 0,0,0,1,2,10,56,495,7376,197398,9803978,902803857
%N A399850 Number of nonequivalent mating graphs on n vertices with connected open-neighborhood family.
%C A399850 Two graphs are equivalent if their open-neighborhood families are isomorphic as set families.
%C A399850 Also, a(n) counts nonequivalent connected nonbipartite mating graphs on n vertices.
%H A399850 I. M. Gessel and J. Li, <a href="https://people.brandeis.edu/~gessel/homepage/papers/pd.pdf">Enumeration of Point-Determining Graphs</a>, Journal of Combinatorial Theory, Series A 118 (2011), 591-612.
%e A399850 a(3) = 1, since K_3 is the only connected nonbipartite mating graph on 3 vertices.
%Y A399850 Cf. A399827.
%K A399850 nonn,more,new
%O A399850 0,5
%A A399850 _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 13 2026
